messages:
marta: Heads-up — our sample app (Node) fails hitting the admin keys endpoint that the REST API uses. curl against /v1/admin/keys works fine, SDK call errors out. Anyone seen this?
alex: which SDK version? stack trace?
marta: v0.9.3, error from SDK: '403 Unauthorized' but same API key works with curl. No stack trace, just the client error.
sam: fwiw we recently gated some admin endpoints behind an enterprise flag in the SDK surface to avoid accidental usage. sounds like parity gap.
alex: also noticed a retry behavior mismatch yesterday: REST returns 503 + x-retry-after and our sample app politely waits; SDK auto-retries immediately without honoring header, leading to duplicate side-effects. Could be related.
marta: repro steps I used: 1) set REDWOOD_API_KEY to personal key 2) run `node sample-app/admin-sync.js` 3) get 403 from SDK client. When I replace sdk call with `curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $KEY" https://api.redwood.ai/v1/admin/keys` it returns 200 and list.
alex: can you paste the snippet?
marta: sure —
```js
// sample-app/admin-sync.js
const R = require('@redwood/inference');
const client = new R.Client({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY });
await client.admin.listKeys(); // -> throws 403
```
sam: thanks. I missed wiring admin routes into the public SDK export in the last refactor. I'll open a PR to expose `admin` when feature flag present and add a runtime check to return clearer error when missing.
devex-bot: Note: onboarding guide currently shows sample app using SDK for admin calls. If SDK lacks admin parity it misleads new users.
alex: for the retry thing — we should align behavior: SDK should surface `x-retry-after` and let caller opt-in to honor or auto-backoff. Current auto-retry is too aggressive for idempotency-sensitive admin routes.
sam: agreed. Plan: (1) quick patch to restore admin binding in SDK (PR link in a sec), (2) add integration test that runs sample app against local mock that returns 503+x-retry-after and assert SDK respects header when `respectRetryAfter: true` option set, (3) update onboarding docs to not show admin usage for free-tier keys.
marta: sounds good. can you add a tiny minimal test I can run locally?
sam: yep — here's a minimal mocha-style snippet you can drop in tests/devex/admin-retry.test.js:
```js
it('honors x-retry-after when option enabled', async () => {
  const client = new R.Client({ apiKey: 'test', respectRetryAfter: true, baseURL: mockUrl });
  await mockServer.onceResponse({ status: 503, headers: { 'x-retry-after': '1' } });
  const start = Date.now();
  await client.admin.doSomething(); // should wait ~1s before retrying
  assert(Date.now() - start >= 1000);
});
```
alex: :thumbsup: once the PR is up ping #eng-runtime and I'll help review the retry bits. Also update sample app to fallback to curl example in onboarding until fixed.
ops-bot: deploy-check: canary job queued for patch branch.
sam: PR 7842 opened: backfill admin export + retry option. Added test and docs note. Link: https://github.com/redwood-inference/sdk/pull/7842
marta: testing now with PR branch — thanks team.
